      "content": "hey i've been hearing this weird low-frequency hum/static in my apartment lately. it's almost like a rhythmic pulsing? i was looking at the weather data for nov 17 2025 and noticed some crazy atmospheric pressure shifts. is it actually possible for certain atmospheric conditions to allow for low-frequency data transmission through the air? like could static actually be carrying encoded info?",
